WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.357 --> 00:00:02.854
- I feel like the name,
vada pav, is exactly

00:00:02.854 --> 00:00:05.447
how feel when I take a bite.

00:00:05.447 --> 00:00:07.094
- It's like vada pav!

00:00:07.094 --> 00:00:10.261
(lively Indian music)

00:00:11.332 --> 00:00:14.243
I've had Indian food before,
but never street food.

00:00:14.243 --> 00:00:16.564
- I don't really know what
to expect with street foods.

00:00:16.564 --> 00:00:18.920
'Cause when I go to a restaurant
there are a lot of sauces.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:21.005
- Maybe it'll be something
that you can hold,

00:00:21.005 --> 00:00:23.317
and walk with easier than a curry.

00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:25.319
- There's probably gonna be spice in it.

00:00:25.319 --> 00:00:26.688
I'm expecting that.

00:00:26.688 --> 00:00:29.994
- Street food is usually
fast, casual, spicy.

00:00:29.994 --> 00:00:31.978
- Yeah, I'm not sure what to expect.

00:00:31.978 --> 00:00:35.104
And I think that's part of the
curiosity of it all, is that

00:00:35.104 --> 00:00:37.521
what would be the difference?

00:00:39.089 --> 00:00:40.185
- Ah yeah.

00:00:40.185 --> 00:00:41.018
- Oh, yes.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.067
- This looks so good.

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:45.829
- Fried, already great.

00:00:45.829 --> 00:00:48.388
(moans)

00:00:48.388 --> 00:00:49.501
- Oh my god.

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:52.913
- There's some red spice, creamy potatoes

00:00:52.913 --> 00:00:57.080
on the inside, a nice hard,
crispy fry on the outside.

00:00:58.679 --> 00:01:01.482
- The sauce is kind of sweet,
which makes it really nice.

00:01:01.482 --> 00:01:03.570
- It's like an upgraded hashbrown.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:04.668
- This is so good.

00:01:04.668 --> 00:01:07.317
(laughs)

00:01:07.317 --> 00:01:09.650
- Wow, it's a big Mac.

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:11.045
- It is so good.

00:01:11.045 --> 00:01:12.681
- Oh my God.

00:01:12.681 --> 00:01:14.283
- I think this is one of the best things

00:01:14.283 --> 00:01:15.942
I've ever put in my mouth.

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.607
I'm not shitting you.

00:01:17.607 --> 00:01:18.605
This is...

00:01:18.605 --> 00:01:19.611
(bleep)

00:01:19.611 --> 00:01:20.619
Beautiful.

00:01:20.619 --> 00:01:21.962
- There's a spice, but a sweetness,

00:01:21.962 --> 00:01:23.913
and then a kick from the onion, like...

00:01:23.913 --> 00:01:26.710
This was very well
thought out, flavor wise.

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:27.761
- This is spicy for me.

00:01:27.761 --> 00:01:29.625
My mouth is on fire right now.

00:01:29.625 --> 00:01:33.065
But I wanna keep eating
it, because it's so good.

00:01:33.065 --> 00:01:34.254
- You feel it there.

00:01:34.254 --> 00:01:36.678
(hums)

00:01:36.678 --> 00:01:38.036
- It's just such an insult, because it's

00:01:38.036 --> 00:01:41.415
like for a McDonald's
burger to be two bucks,

00:01:41.415 --> 00:01:45.352
and this is 60 cents
in India, like get out.

00:01:45.352 --> 00:01:46.688
'Cause a McDonald's burger doesn't

00:01:46.688 --> 00:01:48.442
even have half the flavor.

00:01:48.442 --> 00:01:49.500
- You know what, they should have this

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.333
for sale outside every bar, in LA.

00:01:53.466 --> 00:01:54.716
- In the world.

00:01:56.463 --> 00:01:57.821
- This already looks like something a

00:01:57.821 --> 00:02:00.417
health food store could sell for $15.

00:02:00.417 --> 00:02:01.716
- There's a lot going on in here.

00:02:01.716 --> 00:02:03.072
- Yeah, it's like puff rice, yeah.

00:02:03.072 --> 00:02:04.066
- Chickpeas.

00:02:04.066 --> 00:02:05.061
- [Man] Chickpeas, onions.

00:02:05.061 --> 00:02:06.081
- Some kind of cracker.

00:02:06.081 --> 00:02:07.650
- Oh, it's cold.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:09.396
I don't know why I expect it to be hot.

00:02:09.396 --> 00:02:10.400
- It's very sweet.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.445
- But it's like sweet, but
refreshing at the same time.

00:02:12.445 --> 00:02:14.625
- Each bite is just a
kaleidoscope of flavors.

00:02:14.625 --> 00:02:16.329
- It's like a fried rice potato salad.

00:02:16.329 --> 00:02:18.458
- It does remind me of
a fancy salad, right?

00:02:18.458 --> 00:02:19.476
- Yeah.

00:02:19.476 --> 00:02:21.062
- But then it's got this
sweet tamarind flavor

00:02:21.062 --> 00:02:23.638
that I'm not expecting.

00:02:23.638 --> 00:02:24.635
- It was...

00:02:24.635 --> 00:02:26.366
I mean, it was great, because it was...

00:02:26.366 --> 00:02:28.419
They were all things
I'd never tried before.

00:02:28.419 --> 00:02:30.945
- And they gave me a newfound
respect for vegetarian food.

00:02:30.945 --> 00:02:32.450
I mean, this was all...

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:34.298
These all didn't have meat in it.

00:02:34.298 --> 00:02:36.246
And, they were delicious.

00:02:36.246 --> 00:02:39.038
- I don't know why I was
expecting cone stuff.

00:02:39.038 --> 00:02:40.041
Doesn't make any sense.

00:02:40.041 --> 00:02:41.460
I was expecting curry in a cone.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:42.457
I don't know.

00:02:42.457 --> 00:02:43.716
- I feel like I'm just wrapped up in

00:02:43.716 --> 00:02:45.354
a bunch of blankets, and there's puppies

00:02:45.354 --> 00:02:46.542
giving me kisses.

00:02:46.542 --> 00:02:47.981
- Ah.

00:02:47.981 --> 00:02:49.004
- Great drunk food.

00:02:49.004 --> 00:02:50.000
- I am so happy.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.313
Best taste test ever.
- Yeah.

00:02:51.313 --> 00:02:52.491
- So delicious.

00:02:52.491 --> 00:02:55.436
- I'd really wanna try
Indian street desserts.

00:02:55.436 --> 00:02:58.479
- Comment below if you'd
like to see us try.

00:02:58.479 --> 00:03:01.646
(lively Indian music)

